mh2lm: preflight PMIC-arb battery IRQ routing (0122)

The battery source still relies exclusively on its observer timer (two seconds
in temporary 0121), rather than a hardware event. PM8150B exposes
USBIN_PLUGIN and CHG_STATE_CHANGE through the SM8150 PMIC-arb (GIC SPI 481),
but the port must not claim that shared interrupt or alter peripheral IRQ
configuration before the live APID routing is known.

Add an opt-in `sweetbattirqdiag=1` preflight.  It reads and logs all APID
mappings for PM8150B USBIN (PPID 0x213) and CHGR (0x210), their write owner,
IRQ-owner flag, EE0 owner bitmap bit, and v5 channel enable/status words.
It never registers a GIC handler, enables or clears a PMIC interrupt, writes a
PMIC register, or changes published battery properties.  The default boot path
is unchanged.

